  "about": "Cross-check cases for the mortgage overpayment engine (src/calculators/mortgage, slice M1), from the owner's real mortgage statement or a lender's overpayment illustration. Every case is a todo until filled. Never fill a figure from Sumyard's own engine or from memory. Once M1 exists, its crossChecks test shows an unfilled case as a todo and compares a filled one with the engine.",
  "privacy": "This repository is public. Enter figures only: amounts, rates, dates and month counts. No name, address, account or mortgage number, lender reference, property details or anything else that identifies a person or a loan. In source, name the kind of document and the lender (\"annual statement, <lender>, 2026\") at most; keep the document itself off the repository.",
  "howToFill": "Inputs as the page will store them: amounts as pounds strings (\"123456.78\"), rates as percentage text (\"4.29\"), startDate as YYYY-MM-DD, months as whole numbers counted from the start date (month 1 is the first payment), repaymentType 'repayment' or 'interest-only', interestMethod 'daily' or 'monthly' and dayCount 'actual/365' or 'actual/actual' only if the document states them (otherwise null: the case then tests which method matches), effect 'reduce-term' or 'reduce-payment', lumpSums as [{\"month\": n, \"amount\": \"pounds\"}], and either allowanceRate or allowanceAmount. Fill in expected only what the document shows; leave the rest null. Add source and checkedOn (YYYY-MM-DD), both required once any expected value is filled. tolerancePence is the largest difference accepted; change it only with a note in docs/worked-examples.md.",
